      <activity id="aec6a9c8-4666-58fe-a1f4-94b186712635" activityNameId="ee2de746-c9af-5d33-b9f6-0c7e6c4c817c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Steel, electric, un- and low-alloyed, for reinforcing steel, import to CH, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Steel, electric, un- and low-alloyed, for reinforcing steel, import to CH, at plant
This process was created based on the following process: "Steel, electric, un- and low-alloyed, at plant {RER}".
In comparison to the previously mentioned RER process, the electricity mix was transitioned to the Polish mix. The remainder of the process is consistent with the RER process.

Description of the general RER process:
The new data for the process update was taken from the publication by the European Commission 2013 with the Best Available Techniques (BAT) for iron and steel production (Remus, 2013). This process produces secondary steel. Only scrap is used as iron bearing input 
UUID: 0df78c47-e325-4bbb-bc04-8c450975f7ca
Location: Data relate to plants in Poland.
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: 
Production volume: 
Sampling: Data from literature 
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: 
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_0df78c47-e325-4bbb-bc04-8c450975f7ca.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
